WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.003 --> 00:00:06.028
IIIF Kasane (Curation) — Picking the use case

2
00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:16.705
IIIF Kasane is a viewer that reads IIIF manifests and shows images, 3D models, audio and video together with their annotations.

3
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:25.395
From the Use cases page, we open this example: the IIIF Curation API sample published by CODH.

4
00:00:25.402 --> 00:00:30.077
It is a small curation that picks eight places from two books.

5
00:00:30.085 --> 00:00:34.760
Press "Open in Kasane" to open the curation in the viewer.

6
00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:43.169
IIIF Kasane (Curation) — Opening the curation

7
00:00:43.181 --> 00:00:48.656
The curation is open. On the right, the Contents tab is shown.

8
00:00:48.677 --> 00:00:54.652
The contents are grouped by book. The first group is from Ehon Mushi Erami,

9
00:00:54.665 --> 00:01:01.690
and the second is from Karaito Soshi. Under each, four selected places are listed.

10
00:01:01.696 --> 00:01:07.996
This link opens the fourth entry. The yellow box marks the selected region.

11
00:01:08.004 --> 00:01:13.229
Entries marked "Target region" point to part of a page, not the whole page.

12
00:01:13.242 --> 00:01:23.292
The pager at the top counts six pages. The same page appears twice, once whole and once as a region, so there are fewer pages than entries.

13
00:01:25.103 --> 00:01:31.378
IIIF Kasane (Curation) — Jumping from the contents

14
00:01:31.381 --> 00:01:38.781
Choose an entry in the contents to go to that page. You stay in the same view, even across books.

15
00:01:40.291 --> 00:01:46.591
First, the first entry from Ehon Mushi Erami. The whole page opens.

16
00:01:49.748 --> 00:01:53.798
Next, page nine from the other book, Karaito Soshi.

17
00:01:56.277 --> 00:02:04.827
Finally, the "Target region" entry on page eleven. The page opens, with a yellow box around the selected region.

18
00:02:06.635 --> 00:02:13.060
IIIF Kasane (Curation) — Opening your own curation

19
00:02:13.063 --> 00:02:22.038
The IIIF Curation API is an extension of the IIIF Presentation API, defined by CODH.

20
00:02:22.043 --> 00:02:31.018
A collection groups whole manifests. A curation instead gathers rectangular regions of pages, across manifests.

21
00:02:31.048 --> 00:02:37.273
To open your own curation, put its URL in the box on the top page and press "View".

22
00:02:37.727 --> 00:02:46.177
Add pos with a number to the viewer URL to open at that entry. In this example it was the fourth.

23
00:02:46.182 --> 00:02:52.232
To browse a curation as a filterable list, use "Search a collection or curation".

24
00:02:52.236 --> 00:02:59.911
The sample curation and the Curation API specification are published on the CODH website.
